stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> PENDING: POST /payments with Idempotency-Key
    PENDING --> SUCCESS: confirm SUCCEEDED or verified webhook
    PENDING --> FAILED: confirm FAILED or verified webhook
    PENDING --> PENDING: order terminated, cancellation flag set, status unchanged
    SUCCESS --> REFUND_PENDING: refund accepted as pending
    SUCCESS --> REFUNDED: refund completed immediately
    REFUND_PENDING --> REFUNDED: refund reconciled as succeeded
    REFUND_PENDING --> SUCCESS: refund failed, attempt reverts to SUCCESS
    SUCCESS --> REFUND_PENDING: late success after order termination, refund pending
    SUCCESS --> REFUNDED: late success after order termination, refund completed

    note right of PENDING
        Durable idempotency key is unique in the database. Reuse with
        the same payload returns the original attempt; reuse with a
        different payload is rejected. Stale PENDING attempts are
        reconciled against the provider, never blindly retried.
    end note

    note right of SUCCESS
        Intended behavior: a payment that settles after its order was
        cancelled or failed is fully compensated. The cancellation flag
        is set while the attempt is still PENDING and is checked when
        the provider result arrives.
    end note

    note right of REFUND_PENDING
        A pending provider refund is reconciled by the scheduled job.
        If the provider later reports failure, the attempt reverts to
        SUCCESS and the refund record is marked FAILED.
    end note
